# Item link visibility sync

**Status:** Implemented. Apply `SUPABASE_ITEM_LINKS_VISIBILITY.sql` in Supabase (after `SUPABASE_ITEM_LINKS_TYPE.sql` and current `get_visible_item_detail`).

## What ships

- `item_links.visibility` (`public` / `friends` / `private`); backfill affiliate → public, else private.
- `items.link_section_visibility` (JSON section defaults) on item upsert.
- `SyncLinkData` upserts `id`, `itemId`, `name`, `url`, `type`, `visibility`.
- `get_visible_item_detail` returns `links` filtered for the public-profile surface: **private never**; **friends** to owner or accepted friends; **public** to anyone who can see the item.
- `ReadOnlyItemDetailView`: own profile still uses local Core Data links; other users use RPC `links`.

## Ops

1. Run `SUPABASE_ITEM_LINKS_VISIBILITY.sql` once.
2. Re-sync items (or edit/save a link) so existing rows get `visibility` pushed.
